---
/** Privacy Policy. Text carried over from the previous single-file site (2.2),
 *  with one correction: the retired Canadian phone number replaced with the
 *  current one, per defect 12.2. Edit here from now on. */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Eyebrow from '../components/Eyebrow.astro';
import ReadAloud from '../components/ReadAloud.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';
---
<BaseLayout page=""
  crumbs={[{ name: "Privacy Policy", path: "/privacy/" }]} title="Privacy Policy | MavelogxDigital" description="How MavelogxDigital collects, uses and safeguards personal information. Compliant with GDPR, PIPEDA, CCPA and CASL.">
  <section class="section container">
    <Eyebrow>Legal</Eyebrow>
    <h1 style="font-size:var(--fs-h1);font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.02em;margin-top:var(--s-2)">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <ReadAloud target=".legal" label="Listen to this page" />
      <div class="legal" style="margin-top:var(--s-5)">
      <p class="legal__meta">Effective Date: May 2026 • MavelogxDigital, Toronto, Ontario, Canada • Compliant with GDPR, PIPEDA, CCPA and CASL</p>
      <h2>1. Who We Are</h2>
      <p>MavelogxDigital is a digital creative agency operating in Toronto, Ontario, Canada. This Privacy Policy governs how we collect, use, disclose, and safeguard personal information obtained through our website and services.</p>
      <p>Data Controller: MavelogxDigital | Toronto, Ontario, Canada | {SITE.email} | {SITE.phone}</p>
      <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
      <p>Information you provide: Name, email address, phone number, business name, project details, and any other information submitted through contact forms, email, or during a service engagement.</p>
      <p>Automatically collected: IP address, browser type, operating system, referring URLs, pages viewed, and access timestamps when you visit our website.</p>
      <p>Cookies: We use only essential functional cookies. We do not deploy third-party advertising or tracking cookies without your explicit consent.</p>
      <h2>3. Legal Basis for Processing (GDPR)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><span>Contract performance (Art. 6(1)(b)): processing necessary to deliver the services you request.</span></li>
        <li><span>Legitimate interests (Art. 6(1)(f)): service communications, fraud prevention, and service improvement.</span></li>
        <li><span>Consent (Art. 6(1)(a)): marketing communications, obtained in compliance with CASL.</span></li>
        <li><span>Legal obligation (Art. 6(1)(c)): compliance with applicable laws.</span></li>
      </ul>
      <h2>4. How We Use Your Information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><span>Deliver, manage, and improve our services</span></li>
        <li><span>Respond to inquiries and fulfill project requirements</span></li>
        <li><span>Issue invoices and process payments</span></li>
        <li><span>Send transactional and marketing communications (with consent)</span></li>
        <li><span>Comply with legal obligations and detect fraud</span></li>
      </ul>
      <h2>5. Sharing Your Information</h2>
      <p>We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information. We share only with service providers under binding data processing agreements, legal authorities as required by law, and successor entities in a business transfer under equivalent protections.</p>
      <h2>6. International Data Transfers</h2>
      <p>We operate from Canada, recognized by the European Commission as providing adequate data protection. For transfers to other jurisdictions, we implement Standard Contractual Clauses or equivalent safeguards.</p>
      <h2>7. Data Retention</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><span>Active client records: duration of engagement plus 7 years</span></li>
        <li><span>Inquiry records: 2 years from last contact</span></li>
        <li><span>Marketing consent records: until withdrawal plus 3 years</span></li>
      </ul>
      <h2>8. Your Privacy Rights</h2>
      <p>GDPR (EU/UK): Access, rectification, erasure, restriction, portability, objection, withdrawal of consent, and right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority.</p>
      <p>CCPA (California): Right to know, delete, opt out of sale (we do not sell data), and non-discrimination.</p>
      <p>PIPEDA (Canada): Right to access and correct your personal information.</p>
      <p>To exercise any right, contact MavelogxDigital@gmail.com. We respond within 30 days or as required by law.</p>
      <h2>9. Cookies, Children, and Security</h2>
      <p>We use only essential cookies. Our services are not directed to persons under 18. We implement industry-standard technical and administrative safeguards to protect your data.</p>
      <h2>10. Changes and Contact</h2>
      <p>Material changes will be posted with a revised effective date. Continued use constitutes acceptance. Contact: {SITE.email} or {SITE.phone}. EU/UK residents may contact their national supervisory authority. Canadian residents may contact the Office of the Privacy Commissioner at www.priv.gc.ca.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
